Subject: [PATCH] Dispatch client association work and release completed radios promptly

An accepted candidate query can wait behind a burst of association capability
and publication commands until its HTTP deadline has already expired. Dispatch
those association phases at admission, using their existing protocol handlers.
Retire confirmed commands before admitting the next FIFO owner in the same
scheduler tick, rather than reserving a finished radio for extra ticks.

Keep command locking, radio exclusion, FIFO ordering, retry periods and native
response validation unchanged. No accepted-query timeout is extended.

Upstream-Status: Pending

